From 6da6dbd49dab1d094af108868486adb36ccca20c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:27:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(post): pattern folders with linear and grid copies
 at the post

Add the PatternDef folder row of the operation list (#3012):

- schema: PatternDef (setup, suppressed, order_mode ByTool/ByPart,
  Linear/Grid kind, members, 1-based disabled copies).
- commands: CreatePatternFolder, EditPatternFolder, SetPatternMembers,
  SetPatternInstanceEnabled, DeletePatternFolder (ungroups).
  ReorderOperation and RenameOperation take folders; a member moves only
  inside its folder. DeleteOperation / DeleteEntity take a deleted
  member out of its folder, and undo puts it back.
- cl: transform::copies joins translated copies of a path with rapids
  over the clearance plane; cycle anchors and compensated spans follow.
- post: by tool, one section per member over every enabled copy (one
  tool change); by part, every member at one copy, then the next. A
  turned or flipped WCS, a gone member and a broken row order refuse by
  name. The gate checks each shifted copy against the machine travel and
  the fixtures; a not-judged line names the copies the stock sim skips.
  Per-operation files refuse a by-part folder by name.
- project: a new entity kind `pattern` (older readers refuse it by name).
- MCP: create_pattern_folder, edit_pattern_folder, set_pattern_members,
  set_pattern_instance_enabled, delete_pattern_folder; get_job lists
  pattern_folders; rename_operation and reorder_operation take folders.

Fixes #3012

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
