From 07cd14690ab03f863484a6dc3086ac2927a9f115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:14:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(post): close the pattern folder review findings of PR
 #4423

- model: a pattern folder is not a model (`is_model`), so the model
  list, `get_job` and the laws that ask "has the document a part" do
  not see it.
- project: the load checks the membership law over the whole file. A
  member that is not an operation row, or an operation in two folders,
  refuses the file before any world write.
- post: the plan and the copy gate refuse by name an operation that two
  active folders name. A folder's sections take its members by name,
  not by a count of the rows that follow.
- mcp: a pattern direction entry that is not a number is refused.
- tests: pins for the by-part after-action and setup change (one time,
  after the last copy), and for the copy gate (fixture strike, machine
  travel, clear when the copy is off).

Refs #3012

